.Dd August 30, 2026
.Dt FILEES-WORKER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-worker
.Nd execute one authenticated FileES server action and exit
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm deploy
.Nm
.Cm repository-control
.Ar client-id
.Nm
.Cm whale-v1
.Nm
.Cm upload-reap
.Nm
.Cm upload-seed-reject
.Fl alias Ar realm-alias
.Nm
.Cm mobile-onboard
.Nm
.Cm mobile-proof
.Ar operation-id client-id
.Nm
.Cm mobile-finish
.Ar operation-id client-id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is exec'd once per authenticated deploy or control-plane ticket, dispatching
on its first argument to one of seven subcommands.
.Bl -tag -width "repository-control"
.It Cm deploy
default path, also reached with no subcommand at all; reads a tunnel
session from stdin and runs the desktop/server bootstrap deploy.
.It Cm repository-control
reads one signed control/v1 ticket from stdin scoped to
.Ar client-id
and mutates canonical service-repository records, data repositories,
grants, editing policy or Public Shares channel state, as described below.
.It Cm whale-v1
serves one framed Whale PUT window, status or commit request, as
described below.
.It Cm upload-reap
the operator cron exception described below.
.It Cm upload-seed-reject
plants one harmless EICAR reject in the waiting room of
.Ar realm-alias
so the owner can receive the quarantine projection without a real
infected upload.
Run as
.Sy _filees-state ,
same as
.Cm upload-reap .
.It Cm mobile-onboard
reads a JSON push payload from stdin and stages a mobile client's
activation grant; exec'd by
.Xr filees-entry 8 Ns 's
mobile push branch.
.It Cm mobile-proof
records that a freshly generated mobile installation key proved
possession by connecting; exec'd by
.Xr filees-mobile-v1 8 Ns 's
proof branch.
.It Cm mobile-finish
completes a mobile onboarding operation for
.Ar client-id ;
exec'd by
.Xr filees-mobile-v1 8 Ns 's
finish branch.
.El
It is
.Sy root : wheel
mode 0555 and has no resident service.
The next operation execs the current image.
.Pp
It is the only process that mutates canonical service-repository records,
data repositories, grants, editing policy and Public Shares channel
state.
It publishes through a path-scoped Subversion commit under the shared
service-WC lock.
Unversioned leftovers from a killed older binary are reconciled before
the next scan.
.Pp
In Whale mode it serves one framed PUT window, status or commit request.
It keeps the exact durable offset and immutable generation identity in a
server-owned journal, checks the current client projection, and publishes
only through
.Cm svnmucc
to the reserved
.Pa .filees-whales
namespace.
The worker establishes its own restricted filesystem profile
after the gated session child execs it.
.Pp
Do not run
.Nm
as root against the service working copy.
Root can bypass the 0700 directory mode and then leaves root-owned
pristine objects in
.Pa .svn .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm upload-reap
is the operator exception to the one-shot deploy contract.
It claims ready intake jobs, runs
.Ic upload.av_command ,
and commits a clean payload into
.Ic upload_repo
or copies a rejected payload into the trash tree.
Run it as
.Sy _filees-state ,
never as root:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
* * * * * /usr/local/libexec/filees/filees-worker upload-reap -config /etc/filees/server.json >/dev/null
.Ed
The installer does not install that crontab.
Intake job directories are
.Cm 0770
.Sy _filees-links : _filees-public
so
.Sy _filees-state
(a member of
.Sy _filees-public )
can read them.
.Ic av_command
runs as the reaper user and must be able to open the payload;
.Nm clamscan
does that,
.Nm clamdscan
does not unless
.Sy _clamav
can also read the job directory.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm upload-seed-reject
.Fl alias Ar alias
plants one EICAR test file in
.Ic trash_root
for that realm's waiting room so the owner can receive the quarantine
projection without a live infected upload.
It does not run
.Ic av_command
and does not commit into
.Ic trash_repo ;
the owner list reads the waiting-room filesystem.
.Ic upload-reap
also treats the EICAR test file as infected even when the helper exits 0.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees-client-entry 8 ,
.Xr filees-entry 8 ,
.Xr filees-mobile-v1 8 ,
.Xr filees-service-wc-corrector 8 ,
.Xr filees.conf 5
